From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RK3576 Ubuntu Builder <builder@localhost>
Date: Tue, 26 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] HACK: media: gpu: v4l2: depend on the libv4l2 stubs
 generator

The Rockchip 0003 patch adds the generate_stubs("libv4l2_stubs") target,
and 0004 makes v4l2_device.cc / v4l2_utils.cc include the generated
v4l2_stubs.h, but the v4l2 source_set itself never depends on the stubs
target: only media/capture links it, and only when use_v4lplugin=true
(media/gpu/args.gni defaults it to false).  A Debian-style build without
that flag therefore compiles the v4l2 sources before v4l2_stubs.h exists:

  media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_device.cc:39:10: fatal error:
  'media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_stubs.h' file not found

Wire the dependency where the header is consumed.
---
 media/gpu/v4l2/BUILD.gn | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/media/gpu/v4l2/BUILD.gn b/media/gpu/v4l2/BUILD.gn
--- a/media/gpu/v4l2/BUILD.gn
+++ b/media/gpu/v4l2/BUILD.gn
@@ -131,8 +131,9 @@ source_set("v4l2") {
   deps = [
     ":v4l2_status",
+    ":libv4l2_stubs",
     "//base",
     "//build/config/linux/libdrm",
     "//gpu/command_buffer/service:gles2",
     "//gpu/ipc/common",
     "//gpu/ipc/service",
     "//media",
-- 
